kb/agentic-systems/reviews/swamp.md:52:Extensions package models, workflows, vault providers, datastores, reports, skills, and supporting files under a collective-scoped identity. The registry supplies CalVer versions, release channels, metadata-only promotion, deprecation, dependency resolution, integrity checks, lockfile tracking, and update reporting. Pulled TypeScript is bundled and validated before use; lazy catalogs defer bundle loading until a named type is needed ([extension.md](https://github.com/swamp-club/swamp/blob/cf38c4ec1068613bb7d3432eb74a1ad854156dd7/design/extension.md)).
kb/agentic-systems/reviews/eigenius.md:27:Ordinary `RunProgram` is synchronous. With a persistent backend, it first creates a durable task record; it then evaluates and commits before returning. The recursive evaluator gives explicit order to effectful computation: a let binding's value precedes its body, a component argument precedes dispatch, a function precedes its application argument, a pair's left side precedes its right side, and construction fields follow stored order. The inspected evaluator contains no machinery that discovers independent let dependencies and dispatches them concurrently. That is narrower than the automatic scheduling described in the D3 and D6 design records. This finding does not cover element-level parallelism inside `Map` or `Reduce`, whose helper loop was not inspected. ([program service](https://github.com/eigenius/eigenius/blob/4bc3bb21181ef3736cbbc81f25ae97edf635e9e0/kernel/src/server/programs.rs); [evaluator](https://github.com/eigenius/eigenius/blob/4bc3bb21181ef3736cbbc81f25ae97edf635e9e0/kernel/src/nbe/eval/mod.rs); [D6](https://github.com/eigenius/eigenius/blob/4bc3bb21181ef3736cbbc81f25ae97edf635e9e0/docs/design/d6-execution-architecture.md))
kb/agentic-systems/reviews/agno-agentos.md:93:- Whether coding-agent improvement gets an enforced mutable-path boundary, isolated candidate deployment, full regression before promotion, and automatic rollback.
kb/agentic-systems/reviews/ai-agent-book.md:266:| Definition versus safety policy | The book normatively reserves “self-evolution” for a candidate, independent regression/safety checks, and release gate. Commonplace's [self-improving-system definition](../../theory/definitions/self-improving-system.md) also classifies direct, gateless evidence-responsive self-change, while treating proposal selection as a safer subtype. | This is not advice to deploy gateless updates. It keeps a descriptive membership test separate from the safety architecture used to govern one pathway. |
