kb/agentic-systems/comparisons/memory/memory-systems-table.md:137:| [llmwiki-marimo](../../../agentic-system-analyses/retained/clod--llmwiki-marimo/overview.md) | 2 | Accumulated source/extracted text; wiki prose, collection/index metadata and retained warnings; dataset files; generated aliases and mutable workspace controls including configured prompt text; stored page diagnostics; caller-held history reused by later invocations; optional trace artifacts; Git/index recovery and frozen developer reference copies. Includes their known writes, transformations and later consumers plus locally unresolved initialization, maintenance and evaluator alternatives. Excludes shipped static prompts, unretained current-call results, external provider state/weights and independently unfrozen dependency implementations. | known coverage (The recorded inventory covers file-backed knowledge and controls, SQLite indexes/diagnostics, caller-held history, inspection artifacts and recovery/developer copies. External provider internals are excluded, not classified as accumulated memory.); Source files/cache and extracted source rows/chunks: known — files [wired], sqlite [wired] (Original files and indexed extraction are separate retained parts.); Wiki pages, datasets and configuration controls: known — files [wired] (Markdown/TOML parts are retained files; transient dataset parsing does not add a database store.); Search/reference state and stored verification: known — sqlite [wired] (The indexed content, access metadata and diagnostic scores are SQLite state.); Caller-held conversation and reduced later-turn messages: known — in-memory [wired] (Later turns reuse application-held messages; cross-session persistence is not established.); Trace inspection artifacts, history, snapshots and golden fixtures: known — files [wired], repo [wired], sqlite [wired] (The recorded persistence mechanisms are classified, not universal availability or lossless restoration.) | partial coverage (Human content control and software admission both exist. Initial dataset/workspace admission and unaudited mutation paths remain unresolved.); Ingestion, aliases, diagnostics, repair mutations and trace recording: known — automatic [wired] (A user may start the job; code admits the resulting retained content without per-content approval.); Web submitted content, manual page/control edits and requested historical replacement: known — manual [wired] (The explicit human decision supplies or replaces the retained content at these mechanisms.); Marimo/convenience generated page admission: known — automatic [wired] (Starting save does not make the subsequently generated draft human-approved.); Golden fixture replacement: known — manual [wired] (The operator explicitly chooses the staging snapshot for replacement; code performs the copy.); Initial/external dataset replacement and pre-existing workspace initialization: not-determinable (Generic workspace/file origin does not establish who decided the retained content.); Remaining unaudited repair/evaluation artifact admissions: not-determinable (Known automatic transformations do not resolve all uninspected mutation paths.) | partial coverage (Requested reads and automatic context selection both exist within chains. The request for an answer is not a request for each selected retained part; code selection is a distinct push operation. Remaining maintenance/evaluator internals prevent complete direction coverage.); Model-requested page/search/data tools and operator inspection/restore: known — pull [wired] (Requested material returns are pull; mere code delivery is not another push.); Pre-retrieval evidence and shaped history delivery to answer/condenser models: known — push [wired] (Code selects retained material before the answer invocation, rather than waiting for its retrieval request.); Same-slug existing-page input and retained configuration at later invocations: known — push [wired] (Code selects earlier retained content for generation or config consumers.); Stored diagnostic and frozen fixture reads: known — pull [wired] (Page/lint callers load diagnostic state; development callers load a chosen reference baseline.); Other repair, evaluation packet and feedback read paths: not-determinable (Detailed consumers are not completely inspected; no pull-only boundary or complete union is asserted.) | partial coverage (Signals describe push selectors, not identifiers merely carried by requested files. Coarse and targeted selection remain distinct; unresolved paths are not made inapplicable by known pulls.); Pre-retrieval wiki/source/dataset selection: known — inferred-lexical [wired], identifier [wired], coarse [wired] (Trigger: requested QA turn. Inputs: question or accepted rewrite, aliases/roster, open-page identity and collection intent. Selected parts: chunks, page bodies, dataset rows or key names.); Later-turn history and configured-context delivery: known — coarse [wired] (Trigger: later model/agent invocation. Inputs: available history, refusal/table predicates, tail count and loaded workspace settings. Parts: filtered recent text and configured guidance.); Existing-page selection for ingestion and chat structuring: known — identifier [wired] (Trigger: concept update or same-title draft. Input: generated/selected slug. Part: matching existing page body.); Condenser-mediated pre-retrieval choice: known — inferred-judgment [wired] (Trigger: uncovered follow-up with history. Input: history and question. Part: retained evidence selected after a model rewrite is rechecked.); Remaining maintenance/evaluator automatic selection: not-determinable (Incomplete selector inspection prevents a complete signal inventory; pull file identifiers alone do not supply a push signal.) | partial coverage (Software-admitted chat-to-page writes establish a qualifying trace-fed durable artifact and later consumer. Other included routes do not have bounded absence records; no local or system-wide no is asserted.); Marimo/convenience conversation-to-wiki admission: known — yes [wired] (Recorded conversational turns feed automatic structuring/write and the resulting durable page enters later retrieval or merge.); Human-reviewed web admission and direct human edits: not-determinable (Human content approval is established here, not an automatic trace-fed admission; no evidenced-absence record closes all alternatives.); History reduction and condenser rewrite: not-determinable (Later-invocation context reuse is established, but no durable conversation-summary checkpoint is recorded; this does not support a qualifying positive or bounded negative.); Source ingestion, datasets, aliases and diagnostics/repair: not-determinable (Ordinary source content is not automatically a trace. Its complete origin and all repair/update alternatives are not established as trace-fed or bounded absent.); Raw spans, evaluator outputs, snapshots and frozen fixtures: not-determinable (Raw retention/recovery/reference use alone is not a qualifying automatic durable behavior update. Uninspected feedback and evaluator internals prevent an absence conclusion.) | partial coverage (Authority is consumer-relative. The supported forces below do not establish beneficial activation; uninspected maintenance/evaluator consumers prevent a complete inventory.); Source/wiki/dataset prose and retained conversation at later model/human consumers: known — knowledge [wired] (Inspection rendering is reference use; QA context is not an executable instruction.); Existing page at update models and saved conversation at structuring models: known — learning [wired] (Prior content shapes a durable page update, separately from its downstream evidence role.); FTS content and dataset values at retrieval/projection ranking consumers: known — ranking [wired] (Fixed algorithms can rank using retained operands without learned ranking weights.); Retained configured prompt at agent construction: known — instruction [wired] (Only the user-configured retained prompt part is included; shipped static templates are excluded.); Aliases, fingerprints, blacklist/settings and dataset attributes at scope/grant selectors: known — routing [wired], enforcement [wired], validation [wired] (Each effect is bounded to its inspected consumer.); Verification scores/hashes and retained threshold at diagnostic consumers: known — validation [wired], knowledge [wired] (These classify diagnostic reuse/support, not page truth or universal chat admissibility.); Warning/TODO text and recovery state at maintenance/restore consumers: known — knowledge [wired], routing [wired] (Readable warnings remain advisory while markers and identities drive code decisions.); Frozen golden fixtures at regression/evaluation consumers: known — validation [wired] (The reference baseline checks conformity, not universal factual truth.); Remaining repair/evaluator consumption paths: not-determinable (Every repair, packet/rubric consumer and evaluation feedback path was not audited; no complete authority union follows.) | [AAS-2026-10-18-llmwiki-marimo-58054ccd9ae7-01](../../../agentic-system-analyses/retained/clod--llmwiki-marimo/overview.md) |
kb/agentic-systems/reports/retained-archive/AAS-2026-09-24-rsiagent-01/result.md:521:Implementation conclusion status: wired; operation/effectiveness conclusion statuses: uninspected. Owner/enforcement point for guest isolation: host's AgenticVerifierExecutor and QEMU transaction. Current target selects rollback mirror: guest effects are restored before return, and rollback failure raises an infrastructure error. Remote service effects are outside this contract. Alternate effect-isolated mode invokes private mount/PID/network/IPC/UTS namespaces, checks candidate read-only mounts, and keeps scratch writable. These are distinct deployed dependencies; neither covers ordinary Actor actions or RTE-2 regex-screened checks. Guarantee strength: protocol conditional on host/guest/QEMU contract; deployed isolation remains uninspected. Verifier proposes and decides local correctness; host can reject malformed reports/infrastructure failures; human operators configure or halt the run. Requirement-grounded model investigation is not access to a supplied gold answer. No claim-content oracle beyond the inspected evidence is established.
